# Git workflow

## Commits
- Format: `type(scope): description`, all lowercase.
- type: one of `feat|fix|chore|refactor|docs|test|perf|style|build|ci`.
- scope: short kebab-case area name (e.g. `tasks`, `auth`, `tenant-routes`).
- Optional body after a blank line explaining why.
- One logical change per commit. If the description needs "and", split it.

## Branches
- One feature per branch, created from `main`, named `feat/<short-name>` (or `fix/...`, etc.).

## Pull requests
- The description says what changed, why, and how it was tested.
- Never merge PRs.

## No AI attribution
- No `Co-Authored-By` lines naming an AI tool and no "Generated with ..." lines, in commits or PR descriptions.

## Agent behaviour
- Never run `git commit` or `git push` yourself.
- Instead, propose the exact `git add <files>` and `git commit -m "..."` commands for the user to run.
